The files in this directory are test data from three sources. Each is redistributed under the
terms its source states, which follow in full.

1. re2-search.txt and re2-exhaustive-sample.txt

   Logs of RE2's own tests, built by `make log` in the RE2 distribution
   (https://github.com/google/re2) and taken from the copy Go ships in `src/regexp/testdata`
   (https://github.com/golang/go). re2-search.txt is as Go ships it. re2-exhaustive-sample.txt
   is a part of Go's re2-exhaustive.txt.bz2, decompressed: every 4409th of its cases, counted
   from the first, each written as a stanza of its one string, its one regexp and the line of
   results the log gives the two. Both are under RE2's licence and Go's, sections A and B below.

2. basic.dat, nullsubexpr.dat and repetition.dat

   Glenn Fowler's AT&T regex(3) test data, as Go ships them in `src/regexp/testdata`, where they
   were edited to reflect where RE2 and Go differ from POSIX (each such change is marked
   `RE2/Go` in the file). The data is under AT&T's notice, section C below, which Go's
   `src/regexp/testdata/testregex.c` carries and says covers "testregex.c and all associated
   test data"; Go's edits are under Go's licence, section B.

3. go-find.txt

   The cases of the `findTests` table in Go's `src/regexp/find_test.go`, written one a line.
   Under Go's licence, section B.

